      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "How I'd see this working is having a subset of your Favourites lists with just eight slots, and piping that list out to a special submenu in your radial menu.\n\nDoesn't need to touch your animators or own expression menus at all, just natively handled by the VRChat client itself nice and clean.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-09-16T15:54:01.134Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I'll try to explain this the best I can, essentially instead of trying to cram everything into the one avatar there could be a new feature in the FX layer allowing users to setup a \"Quick Switch\" between two or more avatars instead of having to open the large menu and scroll through to one they needed to use next. I had this thought when thinking about different forms and phases for avatars, this could also alleviate the need to wrangle Unity when two different Forms of an avatar are significantly different physically.",
